1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,027
It works on my machine.

2
00:00:02,027 --> 00:00:03,222
Famous last words.

3
00:00:03,222 --> 00:00:04,749
A teammate pushes code,

4
00:00:04,749 --> 00:00:06,409
and nobody ran the tests.

5
00:00:06,959 --> 00:00:09,631
Two days later a customer pays too little,

6
00:00:09,631 --> 00:00:11,476
because a discount was wrong.

7
00:00:11,476 --> 00:00:12,620
The tests existed.

8
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,893
They just never ran.

9
00:00:14,443 --> 00:00:15,612
The fix is simple.

10
00:00:15,612 --> 00:00:17,300
Let a robot run the tests,

11
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:18,209
on every push,

12
00:00:18,209 --> 00:00:19,508
on a clean computer.

13
00:00:19,508 --> 00:00:20,612
And if they fail,

14
00:00:20,612 --> 00:00:21,781
the robot says no.

15
00:00:22,331 --> 00:00:24,167
Today you build that robot.

16
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:26,003
A GitHub Actions workflow,

17
00:00:26,003 --> 00:00:27,159
with a real gate.

18
00:00:27,159 --> 00:00:28,791
You see a real run fail,

19
00:00:28,791 --> 00:00:30,151
and a real run pass.

20
00:00:30,151 --> 00:00:33,211
And a lab checks your gate by planting a bug.

21
00:00:34,761 --> 00:00:36,190
Here is what to expect.

22
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,831
One: why tests belong in CI.

23
00:00:39,381 --> 00:00:44,458
Two: the anatomy of a workflow file. The trigger, the permissions, the job, the steps.

24
00:00:45,008 --> 00:00:50,320
Three: gates. What makes a run pass or fail, and how to make a gate that cannot be fooled.

25
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:51,944
Then a live demo.

26
00:00:51,944 --> 00:00:53,776
We break the code on purpose,

27
00:00:53,776 --> 00:00:55,166
watch the gate say no,

28
00:00:55,166 --> 00:00:56,366
write the workflow,

29
00:00:56,366 --> 00:00:59,020
and then look at two real runs on GitHub.

30
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:03,879
And a lab with six checks, including a planted bug that your gate must catch.

31
00:01:05,929 --> 00:01:07,529
Why run tests in CI?

32
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:09,466
Because people forget.

33
00:01:09,466 --> 00:01:11,736
And people have different computers.

34
00:01:11,736 --> 00:01:13,691
A pipeline runs the same tests,

35
00:01:13,691 --> 00:01:14,510
the same way,

36
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:15,393
on every push,

37
00:01:15,393 --> 00:01:16,591
on a clean machine.

38
00:01:17,141 --> 00:01:18,374
It gives fast feedback.

39
00:01:18,374 --> 00:01:20,519
The author sees a red cross in a minute,

40
00:01:20,519 --> 00:01:22,986
while the change is still fresh in their head.

41
00:01:23,536 --> 00:01:25,196
It protects the main branch.

42
00:01:25,196 --> 00:01:27,803
Nobody has to trust that the tests were run.

43
00:01:27,803 --> 00:01:29,936
The proof is attached to the commit.

44
00:01:30,486 --> 00:01:31,709
And it is a record.

45
00:01:31,709 --> 00:01:33,511
Every run is saved: the log,

46
00:01:33,511 --> 00:01:34,219
the report,

47
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:34,798
the time.

48
00:01:34,798 --> 00:01:35,635
Months later,

49
00:01:35,635 --> 00:01:38,209
you can see when a test started failing.

50
00:01:38,759 --> 00:01:42,919
Tests that do not run automatically will, sooner or later, not run.

51
00:01:44,469 --> 00:01:49,376
The anatomy of a workflow. A YAML file, in .github/workflows.

52
00:01:49,926 --> 00:01:50,965
On: the trigger.

53
00:01:50,965 --> 00:01:52,135
Run on every push,

54
00:01:52,135 --> 00:01:53,825
and on every pull request.

55
00:01:53,825 --> 00:01:56,944
That way a change is tested before it is merged.

56
00:01:57,494 --> 00:01:59,300
Permissions: least privilege.

57
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,605
Contents read is enough to test code.

58
00:02:01,605 --> 00:02:05,217
A test job should not be able to write to your repository.

59
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:06,751
Jobs: one job,

60
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:07,594
called test.

61
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:09,983
It runs on a fresh Ubuntu machine,

62
00:02:09,983 --> 00:02:11,248
and has a timeout,

63
00:02:11,248 --> 00:02:14,130
so a stuck test cannot run for six hours.

64
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,279
Steps: check out the code,

65
00:02:16,279 --> 00:02:17,141
set up Python,

66
00:02:17,141 --> 00:02:18,248
install the tools,

67
00:02:18,248 --> 00:02:19,110
run the tests,

68
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:20,525
and upload the results.

69
00:02:21,075 --> 00:02:23,238
And pin every action to a version,

70
00:02:23,238 --> 00:02:24,001
like v4.

71
00:02:24,001 --> 00:02:24,891
Never at main.

72
00:02:24,891 --> 00:02:27,308
A moving version can change under you,

73
00:02:27,308 --> 00:02:27,944
overnight.

74
00:02:29,494 --> 00:02:31,649
Now the gates. What makes a run fail?

75
00:02:32,199 --> 00:02:32,821
One rule.

76
00:02:32,821 --> 00:02:37,386
A step fails when its command exits with a number other than zero.

77
00:02:37,386 --> 00:02:40,290
pytest exits with one when a test fails.

78
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,259
The job stops,

79
00:02:41,259 --> 00:02:42,780
and the run turns red.

80
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,551
A coverage gate is the same idea.

81
00:02:45,551 --> 00:02:49,388
--cov-fail-under ninety makes pytest exit with a failure,

82
00:02:49,388 --> 00:02:52,013
if coverage drops below ninety percent.

83
00:02:52,563 --> 00:02:54,115
But watch for the trap.

84
00:02:54,115 --> 00:02:57,626
Adding || true after the command makes it exit zero,

85
00:02:57,626 --> 00:02:58,099
always.

86
00:02:58,099 --> 00:02:59,246
The run is green,

87
00:02:59,246 --> 00:03:00,664
and the gate is dead.

88
00:03:00,664 --> 00:03:03,229
A gate that cannot fail is decoration.

89
00:03:03,779 --> 00:03:04,098
Next,

90
00:03:04,098 --> 00:03:04,737
if always,

91
00:03:04,737 --> 00:03:05,949
on the upload step.

92
00:03:05,949 --> 00:03:06,970
When tests fail,

93
00:03:06,970 --> 00:03:08,821
you need the report the most.

94
00:03:08,821 --> 00:03:09,523
Without it,

95
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,246
the upload step is skipped.

96
00:03:11,796 --> 00:03:12,620
And finally,

97
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:13,788
make it required.

98
00:03:13,788 --> 00:03:15,642
In the repository settings,

99
00:03:15,642 --> 00:03:18,389
a rule can require the test job to pass,

100
00:03:18,389 --> 00:03:20,587
before a pull request can merge.

101
00:03:20,587 --> 00:03:22,441
Then red really means stop.

102
00:03:23,991 --> 00:03:29,068
Go to the lab folder.

103
00:03:30,618 --> 00:03:32,517
Look around.

104
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:34,245
Our pricing code,

105
00:03:34,245 --> 00:03:35,145
cart.py,

106
00:03:35,145 --> 00:03:35,838
six tests,

107
00:03:35,838 --> 00:03:38,194
and an empty folder for workflows.

108
00:03:38,194 --> 00:03:39,233
The gate first,

109
00:03:39,233 --> 00:03:39,787
by hand.

110
00:03:40,337 --> 00:03:46,865
The gate, by hand.

111
00:03:47,415 --> 00:03:48,106
Six passed.

112
00:03:48,106 --> 00:03:51,748
And the line: required coverage of ninety percent reached.

113
00:03:51,748 --> 00:03:51,999
Now,

114
00:03:51,999 --> 00:03:54,135
the number the pipeline will read.

115
00:03:54,685 --> 00:03:56,669
The exit code.

116
00:03:57,219 --> 00:03:59,566
Zero. Success. The step is green.

117
00:04:00,116 --> 00:04:06,644
Plant a bug.

118
00:04:07,194 --> 00:04:09,903
Run the gate.

119
00:04:12,653 --> 00:04:13,296
A failure.

120
00:04:13,296 --> 00:04:13,681
The F,

121
00:04:13,681 --> 00:04:16,444
and the name of the test: the welcome code.

122
00:04:16,444 --> 00:04:16,894
Notice,

123
00:04:16,894 --> 00:04:18,565
the coverage did not drop.

124
00:04:18,565 --> 00:04:20,685
Coverage stays a hundred percent.

125
00:04:20,685 --> 00:04:22,227
The test caught the bug,

126
00:04:22,227 --> 00:04:23,320
not the coverage.

127
00:04:23,870 --> 00:04:25,854
The exit code.

128
00:04:26,404 --> 00:04:29,604
One. Not zero. In CI, this is a red cross.

129
00:04:30,154 --> 00:04:32,756
Restore it.

130
00:04:36,206 --> 00:04:40,772
Where am I?

131
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:46,698
Zero out of six. Nothing exists yet. Honest, and useful: this is your starting line.

132
00:04:47,248 --> 00:04:53,562
Write the workflow.

133
00:05:33,312 --> 00:05:34,080
The trigger,

134
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,104
the permissions,

135
00:05:35,104 --> 00:05:36,576
one job with a timeout,

136
00:05:36,576 --> 00:05:37,280
five steps.

137
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:37,856
Checkout,

138
00:05:37,856 --> 00:05:38,304
Python,

139
00:05:38,304 --> 00:05:39,072
the install,

140
00:05:39,072 --> 00:05:39,648
the gate,

141
00:05:39,648 --> 00:05:40,608
and the upload,

142
00:05:40,608 --> 00:05:41,568
with if always.

143
00:05:42,118 --> 00:05:44,486
Judge again.

144
00:05:45,036 --> 00:05:45,989
Six out of six.

145
00:05:45,989 --> 00:05:47,005
It read my file,

146
00:05:47,005 --> 00:05:47,958
found the gate,

147
00:05:47,958 --> 00:05:51,324
and ran my pytest command twice: once on this code,

148
00:05:51,324 --> 00:05:52,340
where it passed.

149
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:54,753
And once on a copy with a planted bug,

150
00:05:54,753 --> 00:05:56,087
where it had to fail.

151
00:05:56,637 --> 00:06:01,288
The trap.

152
00:06:04,338 --> 00:06:05,532
Judge again.

153
00:06:06,682 --> 00:06:07,659
Five out of six.

154
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:11,018
The last check fails: the gate passes on a planted bug.

155
00:06:11,018 --> 00:06:12,545
The robot would be green,

156
00:06:12,545 --> 00:06:14,682
and the bug would be in production.

157
00:06:15,232 --> 00:06:17,878
Remove the trap.

158
00:06:20,528 --> 00:06:22,853
Judge again.

159
00:06:23,403 --> 00:06:24,811
Six out of six, again.

160
00:06:25,361 --> 00:06:27,324
Clean up.

161
00:06:27,874 --> 00:06:29,730
Removed. Nothing left behind.

162
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,629
Now the same idea,

163
00:06:32,629 --> 00:06:33,903
running for real,

164
00:06:33,903 --> 00:06:34,728
on GitHub.

165
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:38,025
This is a real capture of my own repository,

166
00:06:38,025 --> 00:06:38,775
in Chrome.

167
00:06:38,775 --> 00:06:39,749
Step by step.

168
00:06:40,299 --> 00:06:42,325
I pushed a workflow like ours,

169
00:06:42,325 --> 00:06:43,744
with the bug planted.

170
00:06:43,744 --> 00:06:45,229
Then I pushed the fix.

171
00:06:45,229 --> 00:06:47,390
The Actions tab lists both runs.

172
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:49,416
The first one has a red cross.

173
00:06:49,416 --> 00:06:51,307
The second has a green tick.

174
00:06:51,857 --> 00:06:53,043
Open the red run.

175
00:06:53,043 --> 00:06:54,717
The status says failure,

176
00:06:54,717 --> 00:06:56,042
and the total time.

177
00:06:56,042 --> 00:06:56,599
The job,

178
00:06:56,599 --> 00:06:56,948
test,

179
00:06:56,948 --> 00:06:58,064
has a red cross.

180
00:06:58,064 --> 00:06:58,692
Click it,

181
00:06:58,692 --> 00:07:00,156
and the details open.

182
00:07:00,706 --> 00:07:01,521
Scroll down.

183
00:07:01,521 --> 00:07:01,929
First,

184
00:07:01,929 --> 00:07:03,017
the job summary.

185
00:07:03,017 --> 00:07:06,278
I made the workflow print a coverage table here,

186
00:07:06,278 --> 00:07:07,434
with one command.

187
00:07:07,434 --> 00:07:08,045
Below it,

188
00:07:08,045 --> 00:07:09,133
the annotations.

189
00:07:09,683 --> 00:07:11,415
And here is the best part.

190
00:07:11,415 --> 00:07:12,347
An annotation,

191
00:07:12,347 --> 00:07:14,679
on the exact line of the test file,

192
00:07:14,679 --> 00:07:15,612
line eighteen.

193
00:07:15,612 --> 00:07:16,744
The failing test,

194
00:07:16,744 --> 00:07:17,876
the value we got,

195
00:07:17,876 --> 00:07:19,609
and the value we expected.

196
00:07:19,609 --> 00:07:23,805
A plugin turns a pytest failure into a message on the commit.

197
00:07:24,355 --> 00:07:26,448
Now the log of the failing step.

198
00:07:26,448 --> 00:07:29,782
The coverage line is there: ninety percent reached.

199
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:30,959
A hundred percent,

200
00:07:30,959 --> 00:07:31,286
even.

201
00:07:31,286 --> 00:07:32,790
And yet the run failed.

202
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:33,640
Further down,

203
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,687
the failed test,

204
00:07:34,687 --> 00:07:38,348
and the last line: process completed with exit code one.

205
00:07:38,348 --> 00:07:40,441
That is what turned the job red.

206
00:07:40,991 --> 00:07:42,270
Now the green run,

207
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:43,265
after the fix.

208
00:07:43,265 --> 00:07:44,402
Status: success,

209
00:07:44,402 --> 00:07:45,824
twenty-four seconds.

210
00:07:45,824 --> 00:07:47,103
And at the bottom,

211
00:07:47,103 --> 00:07:49,519
the artifact: the coverage report,

212
00:07:49,519 --> 00:07:50,799
the HTML files,

213
00:07:50,799 --> 00:07:52,575
saved by the upload step,

214
00:07:52,575 --> 00:07:53,855
ready to download.

215
00:07:54,405 --> 00:07:55,451
One more screen,

216
00:07:55,451 --> 00:07:56,759
and it is a setting.

217
00:07:56,759 --> 00:07:58,525
In the repository settings,

218
00:07:58,525 --> 00:08:01,664
a branch rule can require status checks to pass.

219
00:08:01,664 --> 00:08:02,841
You tick this box,

220
00:08:02,841 --> 00:08:04,215
and add the test job.

221
00:08:04,215 --> 00:08:04,934
After that,

222
00:08:04,934 --> 00:08:08,728
a pull request cannot be merged while the test job is red.

223
00:08:08,728 --> 00:08:11,017
I opened this form only to show it,

224
00:08:11,017 --> 00:08:12,325
and did not save it.

225
00:08:13,875 --> 00:08:18,632
Your lab task: write a CI workflow with a gate that really works. Six checks.

226
00:08:19,182 --> 00:08:20,612
One: write the file,

227
00:08:20,612 --> 00:08:21,398
.github,

228
00:08:21,398 --> 00:08:22,541
/workflows/

229
00:08:22,541 --> 00:08:23,899
ci.yml.

230
00:08:23,899 --> 00:08:25,114
It must be valid.

231
00:08:25,114 --> 00:08:26,329
Two: run on push,

232
00:08:26,329 --> 00:08:27,758
and on pull request.

233
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:29,265
Three: Ubuntu,

234
00:08:29,265 --> 00:08:29,949
a timeout,

235
00:08:29,949 --> 00:08:31,042
and permissions,

236
00:08:31,042 --> 00:08:31,999
contents read.

237
00:08:31,999 --> 00:08:33,572
Four: pin every action,

238
00:08:33,572 --> 00:08:35,007
and include checkout.

239
00:08:35,557 --> 00:08:36,965
Five: a pytest step,

240
00:08:36,965 --> 00:08:39,205
with --cov-fail-under eighty or more,

241
00:08:39,205 --> 00:08:40,997
and an upload artifact step,

242
00:08:40,997 --> 00:08:41,957
with if always.

243
00:08:42,507 --> 00:08:44,849
Six: the lab runs your command here,

244
00:08:44,849 --> 00:08:46,997
and on a copy with a planted bug.

245
00:08:46,997 --> 00:08:47,842
It must pass,

246
00:08:47,842 --> 00:08:49,274
and then it must fail.

247
00:08:49,274 --> 00:08:50,250
Then lab check,

248
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:51,616
until six out of six.

249
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:56,461
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

250
00:08:57,011 --> 00:08:58,475
One: the repository,

251
00:08:58,475 --> 00:09:02,795
github.com/it-waves/devops-ai,

252
00:09:02,795 --> 00:09:05,139
in the folder academy/lab.

253
00:09:05,689 --> 00:09:11,769
Two: the files, lab141.sh, and shortcuts141.sh.

254
00:09:12,319 --> 00:09:17,780
Three: install it, with sudo install, into /usr/local/sbin/.

255
00:09:18,330 --> 00:09:20,194
Four: load the short names,

256
00:09:20,194 --> 00:09:23,231
with source shortcuts141.sh.

257
00:09:23,231 --> 00:09:24,060
Then lab up,

258
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:24,750
lab check,

259
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:25,647
and lab down.

260
00:09:26,197 --> 00:09:28,161
Five: you need python three,

261
00:09:28,161 --> 00:09:28,792
pytest,

262
00:09:28,792 --> 00:09:29,703
pytest-cov,

263
00:09:29,703 --> 00:09:31,737
and the python YAML package.

264
00:09:31,737 --> 00:09:34,752
One apt install line gives you all of them.

265
00:09:35,302 --> 00:09:41,062
Six: it only touches /opt/lab141. Lab down removes everything.

266
00:09:41,612 --> 00:09:43,255
The link is in the description.

267
00:09:45,305 --> 00:09:48,953
Pass or fail rubric. Six points. All six to pass.

268
00:09:49,503 --> 00:09:53,343
One: ci.yml exists, and is valid YAML, with a job.

269
00:09:53,893 --> 00:09:56,602
Two: it runs on push, and on pull request.

270
00:09:57,152 --> 00:10:01,099
Three: Ubuntu, a timeout, and permissions with contents read.

271
00:10:01,649 --> 00:10:04,828
Four: every action is pinned, and checkout is included.

272
00:10:05,378 --> 00:10:09,730
Five: a gate of eighty percent or more, and an upload step with if always.

273
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:14,056
Six: the gate passes on this code, and fails on a planted bug.

274
00:10:14,606 --> 00:10:15,907
Pass means all six.

275
00:10:17,957 --> 00:10:19,728
Your turn, on your own machine.

276
00:10:20,278 --> 00:10:25,206
One: lab up, read the task file, and try the gate by hand. Check the exit code.

277
00:10:25,756 --> 00:10:29,681
Two: write the workflow file, with the trigger, the permissions, and the job.

278
00:10:30,231 --> 00:10:32,684
Three: add the steps. Pin every action.

279
00:10:33,234 --> 00:10:36,520
Four: add the gate, and the upload step with if always.

280
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:40,547
Five: lab check, until six out of six. Then lab down.

281
00:10:41,097 --> 00:10:42,932
Pause the video, and begin now.

282
00:10:58,482 --> 00:10:59,357
Quick check.

283
00:10:59,907 --> 00:11:01,485
